use ../../../lib/UiComponent

from ../../../behaviors/Dragging import Dragging
from ../../../behaviors/FormParticipation import FormParticipation

export ui-component AngleSlider:
    description:
        An angle slider is a round dial for setting an angle, such as the
        direction of a shadow or the rotation of a picture. The user turns a
        handle around the dial, and the value is the angle it points at, in
        degrees.

    behaviors:
        - @{Dragging}
        - @{FormParticipation}

    value:
        An angle from 0 up to a full turn. Where 0 points, and which way the
        angle grows, is up to the chosen library.

    pointer:
        The user drags the handle around the dial, and the angle follows the
        direction from the centre of the dial to the pointer. Clicking or
        tapping anywhere on the dial moves the handle to point there.

    keyboard:
        The handle is one stop in the Tab order. The arrow keys turn it by one
        step either way, and with Shift (or the platform's equivalent) by a
        bigger step. Home and End go to the lowest and highest angle. Whether
        stepping past the highest angle carries on round from 0 is up to the
        chosen library.

    steps:
        The component sets the size of a step, such as 1 degree or 15 degrees.
        Dragging also moves in whole steps.

    reporting:
        The component is told about changes continuously while the handle
        turns, and again once when the user lets go, as with a Slider.

    valueText:
        Assistive tools read out the angle with its unit, such as "90 degrees",
        or friendlier text the component gives, such as "East".

    marks:
        Whether it shows marks around the dial, such as every 45 degrees, is up
        to the chosen library.

    disabled:
        A disabled angle slider can't be turned or focused. A read-only one can
        be focused and read out, but not turned.

    nonGoals:
        - No more than one full turn. Values such as 720 degrees for two turns
            are not supported
        - Not a knob for an ordinary number with a start and an end, such as a
            volume. That's a Slider, however round it looks
